# Information Disclosure - Sensitive Environment Variable Exposure via Debug Endpoint

## Executive Summary

An information disclosure vulnerability was identified due to an exposed debugging endpoint within the application.

A hidden HTML comment in the application's homepage referenced a publicly accessible `phpinfo()` page located under the `/cgi-bin/` directory. Accessing this endpoint revealed extensive server configuration details, including sensitive environment variables.

Among the disclosed information was the application's `SECRET_KEY`, which should never be exposed to unauthenticated users.

Although this laboratory only requires retrieving the secret value, exposing debugging endpoints such as `phpinfo()` can leak critical information that significantly facilitates further attacks.

