# Key Takeaways

* Debugging functionality must never be exposed in production.
* HTML comments can unintentionally disclose sensitive internal resources.
* `phpinfo()` reveals extensive configuration data that greatly assists attackers during reconnaissance.
* Environment variables often contain high-value secrets and should never be included in publicly accessible responses.
* Production deployments should be reviewed regularly to eliminate development artifacts before release.
